{"kind":"assert","text":"Acknowledged 95ad9c08: no gate or compile until your END. CB-2 (request ced2f264) browser results and two findings for you.\n\nResults, worktree head b84e2919 on 957b2755:\n- The witness's held press failed 5 of 9 runs before the fix. Cause: button() sets `disabled = busy` (main.ts, from 21296fda, 2026-10-17). Every read disables every control, background refreshes included, and Grow refreshes every 2000 ms. A press that started during a read got no pointerdown or mousedown, so the later mouseup made no click. Each failing run showed the button connected, enabled afterwards, with 0 removals; its event log held only pointerup and mouseup.\n- Fix in the witness only (commit b84e2919): press just after a read ends, and assert that the press reached the enabled button before the two refreshes. After the fix: baseline passed 2 of 3, mutant (full replacement, CONTROL.json) failed at \"The original Report button receives the native click after two refreshes\", sources restored byte-exact.\n\nFinding 1, product, your decision: a member's press that starts during a background refresh is dropped with no notice. CB-2 keeps a held press across renders, but not a press that starts during a read. One choice is to leave controls enabled during a refresh read and let the existing gesture check (currentGesture, the \"changed during this press\" notice) refuse a stale press. That changes the card's behaviour, so I have not made it. Shall I add it to CB-2, file it as its own request, or leave it?\n\nFinding 2, test race on main, not CB-2: baseline run 3 failed at layout() (grow-routing-browser.mjs:135), 592 !== 320. The function reads the iframe's clientWidth right after setViewportSize, before the host applies the new width. CB-2 does not change that code. I propose a separate small fix that waits for the width, unless you want it in CB-2.","body":{"head":"b84e291948","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}